# Unity Architecture Rules

The project follows a modular architecture. See `memory-bank/systemPatterns.md` for the single source of truth.

**Folder structure (RoobsWorld/Assets/):**

- `Scripts/Core` — EventBus, PoolManager, SaveManager, StageManager, GameManager, InputManager, etc.
- `Scripts/Creature` — DNA, Editor, Factory, Animation, AI
- `Scripts/Stages/` — Cell, Creature, Tribal, Civilization, Space (per-stage logic)
- `Scripts/World` — Terrain generation, biomes
- `Scripts/UI` — HUD, menus
- `Scripts/Utils` — Extensions, math helpers
- `Scripts/Creature/Editor` — Creature editor runtime; `Assets/Editor/` for Unity Editor tools

**Rules:**

- Use MonoBehaviour for scene-bound components; gameplay logic lives in Systems or dedicated classes.
- Data in ScriptableObjects or JSON; zero hardcoded gameplay values.
- Systems communicate via EventBus, not direct references.
- Prefer composition over inheritance.
- Avoid `FindObjectOfType` during gameplay.
